Package: god
Title: A Grammar of Data
Version: 0.2.1
Authors@R:
    person("psychometrician", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "psychometrician@gmail.com")
Description: One small vocabulary for manipulating tables, spelled the same way
    in R, in Python, and as plain text. A pipeline is checked whole before any
    of it runs, so a bad column is reported at the step that names it rather
    than failing partway through. The grammar owns the words, the checking and
    the messages; an engine underneath does the work. The manual, live in both
    languages, is at <https://psychometrician.github.io/god-book/>.
License: Apache License (== 2.0)
URL: https://github.com/psychometrician/god,
    https://psychometrician.github.io/god-book/
BugReports: https://github.com/psychometrician/god/issues
SystemRequirements: Cargo (Rust's package manager), rustc
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1)
Imports:
    DBI,
    duckdb
Suggests:
    dplyr,
    knitr,
    pkgload
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.0.0
